"""29 October 2026 : ZenRay Retopology TEMPLATES, components recognised on the model and turned into curves whose quads are perfect by construction.
EN: no hand drawn curve for the parts that are not emergent shapes. Each part of the model is tested against the template library :
  revolution   the part is unchanged by a rotation about one axis (mean distance of the rotated part to itself under rev_tol of its size) ;
  radial N     the part is unchanged by a rotation of 360 / N degrees only (spokes) : recognised and reported, built later ;
The revolution template reads the part's PROFILE (the section by a half plane through the axis, chained into polylines), keeps its corners as
feature points (plus evenly spaced ones on a smooth loop, at least four), and writes the network a modeller would draw : one PARALLEL circle per
feature point and SECTORS meridians, every patch a four sided sector (two circle arcs, two profile pieces) with its four corners named, so the
conversion of ZrlNetMesh gives the lathe grid. Every instance also gets its 2D diagram as SVG (the profile, its features, the sectors).
    python -I ZrlTemplates.py detect [--ref v752]                        the parts each template recognises
    python -I ZrlTemplates.py build --parts wheel --out frag.json         the curve network of the recognised parts (name filter)
    python -I ZrlTemplates.py measure --parts wheel                      build, convert with ZrlNetMesh, print the judge
    POST /templates {"op": "detect" | "build", ...}                       the same for the 3D editor
FR : les components qui ne sont pas des formes émergentes reconnus sur le modèle et changés en courbes dont les quads sont parfaits par construction.
"""
